build(ch, "national-symbols", "National symbols and institutions", 30,
    ["Describe the flag, the motto and the anthem of Cameroon.", "Name the three branches of government in a simple way.", "Say who leads local communities and what a mayor does."],
    [("key", "definition", "National symbols", "The **flag** has three vertical stripes, **green, red and yellow**, with a **yellow star** in the middle of the red stripe. The **motto** is **Peace – Work – Fatherland**. The **anthem** in English begins *O Cameroon, Cradle of Our Forefathers*. The **coat of arms** shows a shield with scales of justice and the motto. We show **respect** for the symbols: we stand when the anthem is played and when the flag is raised."),
     ("fig", fig_flag, "The flag of Cameroon.", "A flag with three vertical stripes, green on the left, red in the middle and yellow on the right. A yellow star is in the centre of the red stripe."),
     ("key", "retenir", "Meaning of the colours", "Textbooks usually say: **green** stands for the forests and hope, **red** for unity, and **yellow** for the sun and the savanna of the north. The **star** stands for unity. The country uses the FCFA as its currency. Yaoundé is the capital."),
     ("key", "retenir", "How the country is governed", "Government has three parts. The **executive** (the **President** and the ministers) runs the country. The **legislature** (the **National Assembly** and the **Senate**) makes the laws. The **judiciary** (the **courts** and judges) applies the laws. Locally, towns and villages have **councils** led by a **mayor** or a **chief** (fon, lamido) who looks after the community and its roads, markets and public places."),
     ("key", "pieges", "Common mistakes", "- Putting the stripes in the wrong order or forgetting the star.\n- Mixing the three branches: the courts do not make laws and the National Assembly does not judge cases.\n- Showing disrespect to the flag or anthem as a joke.\n- Thinking that the mayor and the President do the same job."),
     ("ex", "Example 1", "Describe the flag of Cameroon.", ["It has three vertical stripes: green, red, yellow (left to right).", "A yellow star is in the middle of the red stripe."], "Three vertical stripes (green, red, yellow) with a yellow star on the red stripe."),
     ("ex", "Example 2", "Who makes laws and who applies them to settle cases?", ["The National Assembly (and the Senate) makes laws.", "The courts and judges apply them."], "Parliament makes the laws; the courts apply them.")],
    [M("application", "What colours are the stripes of the flag of Cameroon, from left to right?", "green, red, yellow", ["red, green, yellow", "yellow, red, green", "green, yellow, red"], "Green, red, yellow."),
     M("application", "What is the motto of Cameroon?", "Peace – Work – Fatherland", ["Unity – Strength – Hope", "Freedom – Justice – Work", "Faith – Hope – Charity"], "Peace, Work, Fatherland."),
     M("application", "Which body makes the laws?", "the National Assembly and the Senate", ["the courts", "the police", "the school"], "Parliament makes laws."),
     TF("approfondissement", "The star on the flag is blue.", False, "The star is yellow and stands on the red stripe."),
     MA("approfondissement", "Match the word with its meaning.", [("executive", "runs the country"), ("legislature", "makes the laws"), ("judiciary", "applies the laws in courts"), ("mayor", "leads a local council")], "These are the main parts of government."),
     P("In class the teacher says: 'We are going to raise the flag and sing the anthem.' Eko starts to talk and laugh during the anthem.",
       [PM("How should pupils behave when the anthem is sung?", "stand quietly and show respect", ["talk to friends", "laugh", "run away"], "We show respect to the national symbols."),
        PM("What is the colour of the middle stripe of the flag?", "red", ["green", "yellow", "blue"], "The star is on the red stripe."),
        PM("What is the English opening of the anthem?", "O Cameroon, Cradle of Our Forefathers", ["God Save the Queen", "Arise, O Compatriots", "We are the champions"], "That is the opening line.", points=2)])],
    [("The star on the flag is...", "yellow", ["green", "red", "white"], "It is a yellow star."),
     ("The capital of Cameroon is...", "Yaoundé", ["Douala", "Buea", "Bamenda"], "Yaoundé."),
     ("Who judges cases?", "the courts", ["the National Assembly", "the pupils", "the market"], "Courts and judges."),
     ("A local council is led by a...", "mayor", ["pilot", "judge only", "teacher only"], "A mayor leads the council."),
     ("A motto is...", "a short saying that guides a group", ["a kind of flag", "a river", "a coin"], "Peace, Work, Fatherland is the motto.")],
    [SENS, "Colour meanings and the coat of arms description follow common school textbooks; check wording. Institutions (Senate, National Assembly, councils, courts) described in the simplest way. Anthem line is the English version's first words."],
    prereq=["fslc-social-studies-history-independence"])

